  "text": "Assistant: Let's break down the problem step by step.\n\nFirst, we'll compute the determinant of the matrix \\(\\begin{vmatrix} \\sin a & \\sin b & \\sin c \\\\ \\sin b & \\sin c & \\sin a \\\\ \\sin c & \\sin a & \\sin b \\end{vmatrix}\\). This determinant can be computed using the formula for the determinant of a 3x3 matrix:\n\n\\[\n\\text{det} = \\sin a (\\sin c \\cdot \\sin b - \\sin a \\cdot \\sin b) - \\sin b (\\sin b \\cdot \\sin b - \\sin a \\cdot \\sin c) + \\sin c (\\sin b \\cdot \\sin a - \\sin c \\cdot \\sin b).\n\\]\n\nSimplifying, we get:\n\n\\[\n\\text{det} = \\sin a (\\sin c \\cdot \\sin b - \\sin a \\cdot \\sin b) - \\sin b (\\sin b^2 - \\sin a \\cdot \\sin c) + \\sin c (\\sin b \\cdot \\sin a - \\sin c \\cdot \\sin b).\n\\]\n\nThis can be further simplified to:\n\n\\[\n\\text{det} = \\sin a \\sin b \\sin c - \\sin^2 a \\sin b - \\sin b \\sin b^2 + \\sin a \\sin c \\sin b + \\sin c \\sin b \\sin a - \\sin c \\sin b^2.\n\\]\n\nCombining like terms, we get:\n\n\\[\n\\text{det} = 2 \\sin a \\sin b \\sin c - \\sin^2 a \\sin b - \\sin b \\sin b^2 + \\sin a \\sin c \\sin b + \\sin c \\sin b \\sin a - \\sin c \\sin b^2.\n\\]\n\nNotice that all terms cancel out except for the determinant of the second matrix \\(\\begin{vmatrix} \\cos a & \\cos b & \\cos c \\\\ \\cos b & \\cos c &",
